From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:02:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Treat a media fetch that backed off as a suspended
 download

Net ends a fetch that the media element aborted with success, so a
fetch that was cancelled because the player had enough data ran the
steps for an entirely fetched resource: it fired progress, set the
networkState to NETWORK_IDLE, fired suspend, and queued the end of the
stream in the queue of the cancelled fetch. For a response that gives
no complete length, it also set the input size of the player to the
bytes fetched so far, which the OpenHarmony backend keeps as the size
of the resource.

Such a fetch restarts once the player needs data again, so its download
is suspended, not complete. When the fetch is cancelled for that reason,
queue a media element task that sets the networkState to NETWORK_IDLE
and fires suspend, and ignore the end of its response, which is dropped
anyway when the fetch restarts before it arrives. Queue one that sets
the networkState back to NETWORK_LOADING when the download resumes,
whether at the byte where the player stopped or after a seek, as the
HTML specification asks. No progress event fires in between, since
progress only fires when data arrives.

Fork note: meant for upstream. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: no test; a fetch only backs off once the player's 50 MiB queue
is full. See Validation.

Validation: the setup of the first patch of the series, sampling networkState every 5 ms. With range support, without this patch, networkState turned NETWORK_IDLE at the first back-off, 60 ms into the load, and stayed there while the fetch restarted twice, and progress fired 3 times. With it, it turns NETWORK_LOADING at each restart, 14.5 s and 28.6 s into the load, and NETWORK_IDLE with a suspend event when the restarted fetch backs off again 40 ms later, and progress fires once; with the suspend steps queued at the cancellation instead of the end of the response, as now, the same happens at 13.1 s and 27.1 s, 15 to 40 ms apart. `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 6 --timeout-multiplier 2` of html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements, the-video-element, and html/canvas/element/manual/drawing-images-to-the-canvas and imagebitmap (475 tests) with the series up to the last patch: no new failure; the unexpected results (media_fragment_seek, autoplay-default-permissions-policy, load-removes-queued-error-event) also occur on ohos-main. Re-run with the whole series after the second review: the range case takes 3 requests and 163.2 MB with no seeking event, and the paused case 2 requests, 266.5 MB and a peak of 426 MiB; `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 6 --timeout-multiplier 2` of media-elements, the-video-element and drawing-images-to-the-canvas (449 tests): no new failure; track-cues-seeking timed out in 1 of 13 isolated runs both with the series and on ohos-main, and video_loop_base passed 3 of 3 isolated runs either way. `./mach check --ohos` passes.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
